:{"accessibility":["The tab is a region named by its heading; the coverage line is a status region. The filters are a group named \"Show requirements\" and each one reports whether it is pressed.","A requirement's state is carried by its word and icon, never by color alone; IDs are not translated and are marked as such for translation tools."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Rail, NavItem, Button, Stack, Text, Badge, Alert, SegmentedControl, Segment, TabBar and TabBarItem); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog. The shell is the one of the Overview View.","The filters are a SegmentedControl in the pills look with the count as the Segment badge, the real ones are outline buttons with the count beside the label; the references are link buttons, the real ones are links.","The strings of the app are copied under the same Locale keys; parameters are the Widget values. The six requirements are sample content (requirements.sample.*): their statements paraphrase the kind of Rule a source holds and are not Rules of this repository.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member opened the Overview of a Workspace whose requirement source is the spec kind and chose Requirements (?tab=requirements); the tab exists only then, and Views, Checks, Decisions and Activity are the other tabs.","The base state is a source that was read: the coverage line, the four filters with their counts and a list of six sample requirements (two noUi, two referenced, two unreferenced). Variants filter the list and show a source that is loading, could not be read, cannot be read at all, has no requirement, or lacks the IDs that Views reference.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the Workbench chrome follows the Workbench language, so its text is baked here per Locale. The requirement IDs, statements and reasons are sample content of a requirement source, not translated."],"intent":"Show the Requirements tab of the Overview as built from Adapter Widgets only: every requirement of the Workspace's requirement source as referenced, unreferenced or noUi with its reason, the IDs that no source Rule has, and the coverage, each linked to the Views, Variants and UX Flows that reference it.","interactionRules":["Each requirement shows its state (Referenced, Unreferenced or noUi), its ID and its statement; a noUi requirement keeps its reason visible, a referenced one lists the Views, Variants and UX Flows that reference it as links, and an unreferenced one says nothing references it yet.","The coverage line gives the share of the source's requirements that are not noUi and that at least one View, Variant or Flow references, with the two counts; a requirement marked noUi is outside coverage whatever references it. A source with nothing to cover says so instead of giving a share.","The filters show All, Referenced, Unreferenced and noUi with their counts and keep one in effect; a filter with no requirement says so. IDs that the Workspace references but the source has no Rule for are listed apart, with where they are referenced, and kept as written.","A source that cannot be read is never shown as coverage: the tab says so and lists the referenced IDs as unverified; a read that failed says so with Try again.","The tab only presents: an agent writes references and noUi marks through MCP."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"opened-from","type":"view","viewId":"2e2f88d6-7a95-424a-b3d4-4661d811ef13"}],"requirements":["01a18120-feff-713c-b556-6511fad1a0d5","01a18120-fd5d-7226-bc8c-5aabd117ce88","01a18120-fde6-7fae-bc6f-c5ceffe81b12"]},"variants":{"filter-noui":{"requirements":["01a18120-fde6-7fae-bc6f-c5ceffe81b12"],"state":{"filter-all":{"selected":false},"filter-noui":{"selected":true},"filter-referenced":{"selected":false},"filter-unreferenced":{"selected":false},"req-noui1":{"visible":true},"req-noui2":{"visible":true},"req-ref1":{"visible":false},"req-ref2":{"visible":false},"req-unref1":{"visible":false},"req-unref2":{"visible":false}}},"filter-referenced":{"state":{"filter-all":{"selected":false},"filter-noui":{"selected":false},"filter-referenced":{"selected":true},"filter-unreferenced":{"selected":false},"req-noui1":{"visible":false},"req-noui2":{"visible":false},"req-ref1":{"visible":true},"req-ref2":{"visible":true},"req-unref1":{"visible":false},"req-unref2":{"visible":false}}},"filter-unreferenced":{"state":{"filter-all":{"selected":false},"filter-noui":{"selected":false},"filter-referenced":{"selected":false},"filter-unreferenced":{"selected":true},"req-noui1":{"visible":false},"req-noui2":{"visible":false},"req-ref1":{"visible":false},"req-ref2":{"visible":false},"req-unref1":{"visible":true},"req-unref2":{"visible":true}}},"load-failed":{"state":{"coverage":{"visible":false},"load-failed":{"visible":true},"req-body":{"visible":false}}},"loading":{"state":{"coverage":{"visible":false},"coverage-loading":{"visible":true},"req-body":{"visible":false}}},"no-coverage":{"state":{"coverage":{"visible":false},"coverage-none":{"visible":true},"filter-row":{"visible":false},"req-empty-source":{"visible":true},"req-list":{"visible":false}}},"no-match":{"state":{"filter-all":{"selected":false},"filter-noui":{"selected":true},"filter-referenced":{"selected":false},"filter-unreferenced":{"selected":false},"req-empty":{"visible":true},"req-list":{"visible":false},"req-noui1":{"visible":false},"req-noui2":{"visible":false},"req-ref1":{"visible":false},"req-ref2":{"visible":false},"req-unref1":{"visible":false},"req-unref2":{"visible":false}}},"unavailable":{"requirements":["01a1814f-8133-7965-9e91-df5fa1f83b53"],"state":{"coverage":{"visible":false},"req-body":{"visible":false},"unavailable":{"visible":true},"unve